# The Red Hand's leaders: the boss at the stronghold and the crew bosses.
# Voice: mocking, casual, always counting. Rudi's end is never a joke; the official lie is said flatly.
# Lines are spoken straight to the player (docs/WRITING.md, "Conversations"): who they are, where
# you are and what's going on, in their own words.

# The first time you meet one (a greet: the talk screen opens on it). One line, said only to a
# stranger (!met); the season's name (names.rzd) and a caught lie come first when they apply.
conv redhand.leader.hello
for stronghold:redhand, seat:redhand/crew_boss
when !met
greet
once
prio flavour
voice redhand

node start
  say? stronghold & !met :: I'm {npc}, {role}. That's the book on the desk. Every crew on every road pays into it. Guns stay quiet in camp, and anything you want has a price. Pull up a chair.
  say? kit:other & !met :: I'm {npc}, {role}. You walked into a Red Hand camp in somebody else's colours. Brave. The lads have a bet on whose jacket it was.
  say? !met :: I'm {npc}, {role}. This is a Red Hand camp. This stretch of road is ours, and so is the toll on it. Guns stay quiet in camp. Want something? Everything's got a price.

conv redhand.leader.book
for stronghold:redhand, seat:redhand/crew_boss
topic "What's that book you keep?"
prio world
voice redhand

node start
  say The book. Who owes, who's owed, and whose it was before they paid with it. Every crew on every road pays its cut, and every cut goes in here.
  say It has to balance. That's not the same as anyone being paid up. Nobody's ever out of the book. A man who owes nothing can walk away, and then where's your road?
  > @first What's the first line in it? -> first
  > @mine What does it say about me? -> mine
  > @other Let me ask about something else. -> hub

node first
  say Day 2. Ten litres of diesel, on tick. Next to it, one word: paid. The pumps were dry that day. Rudi had a garage at the crossroads, and the key to the tank under the forecourt.
  say? stronghold :: My handwriting. Still neat. I was trying, back then.
  say Before my time. Ask the boss. Actually, don't.
  > @rudi What happened to Rudi? -> rudi
  > @back1 Let me ask about something else. -> hub

node rudi
  say? stronghold :: He let people pay later. You can't run a road like that.
  say Rudi was bitten.
  > @back2 I see. Something else. -> hub

node mine
  say Show you your own page? That's not how the book works. The book gets read to you, when the boss picks the moment, usually in front of people.
  > @look Go on. Show me anyway. -> shown | teased | shut   check persuade redhand 2 harder:paranoid bg:excon,raider
  > @leave1 Keep it, then. -> hub

node shown
  say Fine. You've got a page, and it's not blank. Here's what it says, word for word.
  do call:standing
  > @back3 Thanks. Let me ask something else. -> hub

node teased
  say Two lines. One of them's a number. Come back when you're worth a third, and I'll read you all three.
  > @back4 I'll hold you to that. -> hub

node shut
  say The book's for reading out loud, at the right moment. This isn't it. You'll know the moment when it comes. Everybody does.
  > @back5 Then something else. -> hub

conv redhand.leader.toll
for stronghold:redhand, seat:redhand/crew_boss
topic "Why is the hand painted red?"
prio flavour
voice redhand

node start
  say Red hand means stop. Stop means pay. Pay means we're friends. See? Easy. Every roadblock with a hand on it takes a tin or a can of fuel, and you drive on.
  say Bastion paints signs, all words and arrows. We paint one sign, and everybody in the Zone can read ours.
  > @paint Who painted the first one? -> paint
  > @other2 Let me ask about something else. -> hub

node paint
  say The boss. On a garage shutter at the crossroads, Day 7, right over some marks that were already there. The crews call it Rudi's shutter.
  say Nobody asks about the marks. People who ask about the marks get a page.
  > @back6 Then I won't ask. -> hub
